            <ArticleTitle>Late drug-eluting stent thrombosis and erythropoietin: cause and effect?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>305-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of late thrombosis of a sirolimus-eluting stent, 16 months after implantation, is described. Two weeks prior to presentation with stent thrombosis the patient had a 50% dose increase of longterm erythropoietin. The prothrombotic effect of erythropoietin may have precipitated the thrombotic event.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
